# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sage OPERATOR TOOLING environment — copy to `.env` at the repository root (gitignored).
#
#   cp .env.example .env          # fill in the paths for your machine
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a      # load it into your shell before running skill scripts
#
# NOTE: nothing auto-loads this file. The skills read these values from the ENVIRONMENT, so you must
# export them (the two-liner above does it for a shell session). This is deliberate: an implicit
# dotenv loader in a repo that also ships a container `.env` is a foot-gun waiting to fire.
#
# THIS IS NOT `Payload_Type/sage/.env`. The two files are unrelated and must not be merged:
#
#   Payload_Type/sage/.env   Sage's own RUNTIME environment — read by the Sage process, whether it
#                            runs in the Mythic container or locally in tmux. Holds DEBUG_LEVEL,
#                            MYTHIC_SERVER_HOST, RABBITMQ_HOST, RABBITMQ_PASSWORD, AWS_* (Bedrock),
#                            SAGE_RUN_AS_PASSWORD, and SAGE_BLOODHOUND_MCP_DIR. Changing it changes
#                            how Sage behaves at runtime.
#
#   .env  (this file)        Where the OPERATOR SKILLS find things on *your* machine. Read only by
#                            tooling under `skills/` — resets, payload deploys, live runners, eval
#                            harnesses. Never read by the Sage container. Changing it changes where
#                            your tools look; it cannot change Sage's behavior.
#
# ── Why there are no defaults ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The tooling does NOT guess where your Mythic or BloodHound checkouts live. It used to probe for
# sibling directories by name, which meant the repository carried one maintainer's directory names
# as source. Every path below is explicit or the tool fails closed and names the variable to set.
#
# That means Mythic-facing tooling needs configuration before first use. That is the intended
# trade: a loud "set MYTHIC_ENV_PATH" beats silently reading the wrong install, which is exactly
# what a name-guessing probe does when you keep more than one Mythic checkout around.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Mythic ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute path to your Mythic install's .env. Required by Mythic-facing tooling unless you set
# MYTHIC_ADMIN_PASSWORD below instead.
MYTHIC_ENV_PATH=

# Mythic admin password. Checked BEFORE MYTHIC_ENV_PATH, so setting this alone is enough to
# authenticate without pointing at a Mythic checkout. Prefer it in CI and on tooling-only hosts.
MYTHIC_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Path to the `mythic-cli` binary, used by the reset tooling to stop/start/reset Mythic.
#
# If you keep more than one Mythic install, set this and MYTHIC_ENV_PATH to the SAME install.
# Setting only MYTHIC_ENV_PATH points the API clients at one install while the reset script drives
# whatever MYTHIC_CLI resolves to — a split-brain reset that looks like it worked.
MYTHIC_CLI=

# ── BloodHound: NOT here ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAGE_BLOODHOUND_MCP_DIR is Sage RUNTIME config, not operator-tooling discovery — the running Sage
# process reads it to auto-connect the BloodHound MCP at startup (ai/bloodhound_config.py), and the
# container image bakes its own `ENV SAGE_BLOODHOUND_MCP_DIR=/opt/bloodhound_mcp`.
# It therefore belongs in the runtime env file, `Payload_Type/sage/.env`, alongside RABBITMQ_HOST and
# the Bedrock credentials. `sage_restart.sh` reads it from there and fails closed if it is missing.

# ── Target run-as credentials: NOT here ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAGE_RUN_AS_PASSWORD is resolved from `Payload_Type/sage/.env` or `~/.config/sage/runas.env` by
# the launch helpers (foothold_launch.py, launch_apollo_foothold.sh, open_rdp_session.py). Keep it
# in one of those, not here — a credential duplicated across two files drifts.

# ── Evidence relocation (advanced) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Point sealed-evidence readers at an archived bundle instead of the live `.sage_history/` tree.
# Leave empty unless you are reviewing an archive. See docs/development/TEST_TIERS.md.
SAGE_EVAL_EVIDENCE_ROOT=
